</div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/recent_actual_test_3_academic_listening_test_1_3.m4a"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3126164-recent_actual_test_3_academic_listening_test_1_4.m4a","question_groups":[{"id":"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-38","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</p><p><strong>Chimpanzee Behaviours</strong></p><p><strong>Species</strong></p><ul><li>We can find Pan or Pan Troglodytes in West and Central Africa.</li><li>The Bonobo or Pan Paniscus are found in Democratic Republic of Congo.</li></ul><p><strong>Current research</strong></p><ul><li>rule out <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and biological factors</li><li>learn through <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of other chimps' behaviour</li></ul><p><strong>Discoveries</strong></p><ul><li>The book <em>The Third Chimpanzee</em> by James Diamond discusses some physical features of chimpanzees.</li><li>The discovery reported by Jane Goodall suggests that chimpanzees know how to use <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li></ul><p><strong>Chimpanzees in Senegal</strong></p><ul><li>use spears sharpened with their teeth</li><li>can <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> the shell of a coconut</li><li>use a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> hammer to crash nuts</li><li>are capable of learning <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and understanding human language</li></ul><p><strong>Sub-species</strong></p><ul><li>Bonobos live on the other side of a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>Both of them are reducing alarmingly in population <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":8},{"id":"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-g4-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 39-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p><p>Which TWO topics about chimpanzees will the students discuss next week?</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong> Which TWO topics about chimpanzees will the students discuss next week?</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>They are slower than human in different ways.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>They learn things by copying humans' behaviour.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>They develop behaviours generation by generation.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">D</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"D\"></span><span>They have very strong ability of logical thinking.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">E</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"E\"></span><span>They could be modified to adapt to the environment.</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":1}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/recent_actual_test_3_academic_listening_test_1_4.m4a"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-q1","part_id":"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-practice-source-3-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","corre